    "Configured endpoints, public catalogs and web/X/video searches are bounded discovery, not an exhaustive internet crawl. Every keyword-matched candidate in the resulting pools was reviewed against its original source; nothing was auto-imported. The 916 candidates rejected on 2026-10-12 and 2026-10-14 were not re-reviewed, except the Bilibili backlog below (12 GitHub repositories resurfaced and were rejected again).",
    "Bilibili standard changed on 2026-10-15 by user decision: a title or description naming Opus 5.5 as the maker plus a description or cover showing a concrete work is now sufficient. 125 of 178 new Bilibili cases rely on this (attribution=title-only in the review file); their summaries say the uploader does not state which parts the model did. Re-uploads, news, comparisons without a task, promotions and repeated same-format uploads remain excluded. Other platforms still require the model role.",
    "Bilibili backlog: 103 videos rejected on 2026-10-12 or 2026-10-14 only for thin documentation were re-reviewed under the new standard; 78 were accepted (including 48 of the 66 earlier 'version named only in the title' rejections). They are dated 2026-10-10 to 10-13 and recorded as backfill.",
